      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your years of rigorous discipline have finally allowed for that profound letting go, but it is precisely this release that allows for a new kind of life beyond the adrenaline of the operating room. This sensation of emptiness is often the painful, necessary bridge between one era of one's life and another, not a sign of finality but of transition to something deeper and perhaps more peaceful. Please consider reaching out to a trusted friend or a compassionate counselor who can help you navigate this profound shift without the weight of this exhausting expectation.",
      "source": "target",
